    "Condition : 1 - \r\nNot Grant\r\nReasons:\r\nThe London Borough of Hounslow as the Local Planning Authority hereby certify that on7/11/07, the erection of a dormer roof extension measuring 3.7m, (depth) x 2.1m, (high) x 5.6m, (long) and hip to gable 2.7m, (high) x 3.9m, (depth) x 8.1m (width) was not lawful within the meaning of Section 191 and 192 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 for the following reason:\r\nThe development falls outside the provisions of Schedule 2, Part 1, Classes A and B of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) Order because the existing rear extension combined with the proposed roof extension would exceed 70m3.\r\n\r\n"
